stablish. A stated boundary was chosen over relying on each reviewer to infer it, because an inferred boundary varies by session and cannot stop repeated rework. Fed back to the need: SN-006's acceptance could identify the normal working environment in which a review finding is actionable; until it does, this row is derived and says so.\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"The review scope includes repository content agents write, supported configurations, and regressions of supported behavior; one authoritative definition excludes a finding whose reproduction requires a compromised or contrived host; the party that rules an out-of-scope finding records its dismissal in one recorded line in the response to the review verdict and, when the run keeps a delegated-decisions record, in that record too, without a code response; and the enumerated set of delivered briefs that judge a review finding each cite that definition without restating its boundary examples.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"The review scope includes repository content agents write, supported configurations, and regressions of supported behavior; one authoritative definition excludes a finding whose reproduction requires a compromised or contrived host; the party that rules an out-of-scope finding records its dismissal in one recorded line in the response to the review verdict and, when the run keeps a delegated-decisions record, in that record too, without a code response; and the enumerated set of delivered briefs that judge a review finding each cite that definition without restating its boundary examples. Review directions tie every severity class to a scenario reachable through supported workflows or routes: a fail-open, data-loss, or security path counts only when one reaches it, and a rare or contrived path is MINOR at most or dismissed. A contrived scenario uses a forbidden hand act or an ordering no supported workflow or route produces. Whoever rules a finding re-grades a mislabelled BLOCKER or MAJOR. A specification promise over an input space reaches only what supported workflows or routes produce unless it states otherwise. Dispute directions weigh a scenario's plausibility under that promise, not only host compromise or cost. They classify an out-of-set input as a coverage-extension note when it fails closed and as a finding when it fails open; and convergence review confirms fixes, checks Done-when coverage and regressions, tags each new BLOCKER or MAJOR, and treats a new finding as BLOCKER or MAJOR only when it is a reachable fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when gap.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":1807,"oldLines":9,"newStart":1807,"newLines":9,"lines":[" sn_refs = [\"SN-006\"]"," boundary_refs = [\"B-09\", \"B-10\"]"," hat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]","-requirement = \"Where a review finding is contested by the builder or coordinator, or recurs for a third review round, the delivered adjudication content shall preserve each requested finding, the position held on it and its relevant change scope, and accept only a verdict that rules every requested finding exactly once as a fix, a reasoned dismissal in a declared class, or an escalation to the owner.\"","+requirement = \"Where a review finding is contested by the builder or coordinator, or recurs for a third review round, the delivered adjudication content shall preserve each requested finding, the position held on it and its relevant change scope, accept only a verdict that rules every requested finding exactly once as a fix, a successor row, a reasoned dismissal in a declared class, or an escalation to the owner, and direct the dispute sitting to rule out a successor row for a fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when-gap finding.\""," rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-006 asks an unattended run to report failures clearly and surface to a human when it cannot proceed, but it does not state who ends a contested or repeated review finding. The unattended-operations lens listens for an unbounded review loop in which the coordinator sends the same finding back to the builder without a bounded, attributable decision. A complete adjudication was chosen so an independent call can settle each requested finding without silently adding, dropping or defaulting one. Fed back to the need: SN-006's acceptance could state that contested review findings receive a bounded ruling; until it does, this row is derived and says so.\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"A composed adjudication carries exactly the requested findings, each finding and held position verbatim, change-range facts, and a link to the review scope; malformed findings input refuses composition without a partial sitting. A verdict refuses when a requested finding is unruled or ruled twice, an unrequested finding is ruled, a ruling is outside the declared set, a dismissal lacks its declared reason class, or a ruling lacks its reason. An accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"A composed adjudication carries exactly the requested findings, each finding and held position verbatim, change-range facts, and a link to the review scope; malformed findings input refuses composition without a partial sitting. A verdict refuses when a requested finding is unruled or ruled twice, an unrequested finding is ruled, a ruling is outside the declared set, a dismissal lacks its declared reason class, or a ruling lacks its reason. An accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act. A SUCCESSOR ruling has a reason; an unknown ruling names the declared ruling set; and the shipped dispute directions rule out a successor row for a fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when-gap finding.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":1837,"oldLines":9,"newStart":1837,"newLines":9,"lines":[" sn_refs = [\"SN-024\"]"," boundary_refs = [\"B-09\", \"B-10\"]"," hat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]","-requirement = \"When a reviewed change requires rework, the delivered review workflow shall dispatch that rework only after its plan covers, or excludes with a reason, every finding of the review it answers as a clause in the order written; an exclusion based on a dispute ruling resolves a finding only when an accepted dismissal ruled that same finding.\"","+requirement = \"When a reviewed change requires rework, the delivered review workflow shall dispatch that rework only after its plan covers, or excludes with a reason, every finding of the review it answers as a clause in the order written; an exclusion based on a dispute ruling resolves a finding only when an accepted dismissal or successor ruling ruled that same finding.\""," rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-024 requires an independent critical eye to drive rework, but does not say how a rework plan preserves every finding that eye raised. The unattended-operations lens listens for a green because nothing looked: dispatching from a plan that omits, renumbers or substitutes a finding lets the change appear answered while the reviewer's concern received no response. Treating every reasoned exclusion as a resolution was rejected because a disputed finding remains open unless its accepted dismissal decided that very finding; keeping each finding as an ordered clause makes the plan and review commensurable. Fed back to the need: SN-024's acceptance could state that rework answers every review finding.\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"A review verdict or a declared F# findings input produces one ordered clause per finding; dispatch is refused while any clause is neither covered nor reasoned-excluded. An exclusion citing a dispute ruling passes only when its accepted dismissal records the same finding; a dismissal of another finding, another round's same-numbered finding, a finding that cannot be shown, or a non-dismissal ruling is refused.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"A review verdict or a declared F# findings input produces one ordered clause per finding; dispatch is refused while any clause is neither covered nor reasoned-excluded. An exclusion citing a dispute ruling passes only when its accepted dismissal or successor ruling records the same finding; a dismissal or SUCCESSOR ruling of another finding, another round's same-numbered finding, a finding that cannot be shown, or a ruling other than an accepted DISMISS or SUCCESSOR is refused.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3380,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3380,"newLines":9,"lines":[" level = \"Integration\""," method = \"Run the dispute tests that compose a brief carrying every finding, held position, range fact and review-scope link; refuse malformed findings input, including a finding with an extra key and one missing any of id, held_by, finding, or position, each by name without a brief; parse a complete verdict; refuse malformed, incomplete, duplicated, unrequested, or unbound verdicts; prove an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act; and prove the class is routed through its shipped template. Run the coordinator-entry tests that accept the dispute class, bind every requested finding, reject an unruled finding, and refuse a dispute brief naming no findings before launch. Parse a SUCCESSOR ruling, refuse a SUCCESSOR without a reason and an unknown ruling, and bind an accepted SUCCESSOR verdict at the coordinator entry point.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"A dispute brief contains every requested finding and position verbatim with independently derived range facts and a review-scope link, or refuses without a partial brief. A finding with an extra key or one missing any of id, held_by, finding, or position refuses by name without a brief. Its verdict accepts exactly one reasoned declared ruling for every requested finding and no other; an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act. The coordinator entry point binds the requested findings and refuses an empty request before launch. A reasoned SUCCESSOR ruling is accepted and bound at the coordinator entry point; a reasonless SUCCESSOR and any unknown ruling refuse the verdict.\"","+expected = \"A dispute brief contains every requested finding and position verbatim with independently derived range facts and a review-scope link, or refuses without a partial brief. A finding with an extra key or one missing any of id, held_by, finding, or position refuses by name without a brief. Its verdict accepts exactly one reasoned declared ruling for every requested finding and no other; an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act. The coordinator entry point binds the requested findings and refuses an empty request before launch. A reasoned SUCCESSOR ruling is accepted and bound at the coordinator entry point; a reasonless SUCCESSOR and any unknown ruling refuse the verdict. The shipped dispute directions rule out SUCCESSOR for a convergence-class finding: a fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when-gap finding.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_dispute.py::test_the_dispute_brief_carries_each_finding_its_position_range_and_scope_link;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_malformed_findings_file_refuses_the_brief;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_well_formed_verdict_is_accepted_and_parsed;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_malformed_or_incomplete_verdict_is_refused;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_verdict_judged_against_no_requested_findings_is_refused;tests/test_dispute.py::test_an_accepted_dispute_verdict_authorizes_no_approval_act;tests/test_dispute.py::test_the_dispute_class_is_routed_and_its_template_ships;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_the_entry_point_accepts_the_dispute_class;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_a_dispute_verdict_ruling_every_finding_is_valid_and_bound;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_a_disp